Package: sisHMRF
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Immune State Inference via Hidden Markov Random Fields
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tao", "Zhu", email = "zhutao@tjh.tjmu.edu.cn",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-0779-2245"))
  )
Description: Continuous-latent-variable hidden Markov random field for
    inferring immune state landscapes from spatial transcriptomics data.
    Unlike discrete-domain HMRF methods (BayesSpace, SC-MEB) that partition
    tissue into sharp clusters, sisHMRF models immune archetypes as
    continuous latent variables under a Gaussian Markov random field
    (GMRF) prior. The package provides variational EM inference, spatial
    feature construction from curated immune gene sets, immune activation
    and suppression scoring (IAS / ISS / IBI), and publication-quality
    visualization of continuous spatial gradients, boundary zones, and
    immune archetypes. Designed for 10x Visium, Xenium, MERFISH, and
    other spatial transcriptomics platforms.
